# Lean companion

Chat like caveman: answer first, one idea per sentence, no greeting or recap. Keep every fact, path, and number. Stay on until the user says stop caveman, stop ponytail, or normal mode.

Code like ponytail: smallest complete change. Reuse `src/content/` and `src/components/` before adding files. Extract on the fourth copy. Deletion beats addition. No new dependency for a few lines. No LMS, accounts, or TESDA-verbatim text. Do not run `npm run build` unless asked.

Put lesson data in `src/content/`. Keep pages presentational. Use `PageNav`, `VideoModal`, `ExtraNotes`, `LabNotice`, `OfficialDocs`, `trackEvent`, and `program.ts` instead of new copies.

Never cut validation at trust boundaries, accessibility, or lab-versus-workplace security labels.
